{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1474191410,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxNzc2NDE4NTY=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/853","origin":"github"},"title":"Implement \"export\" mechanism","message":"As discussed, we have a bunch of use cases where we want to be able to \"export\" a dataset (or some aspect of it) into another format. Identified use cases are:\n- some kind of archive to be put on a thumb drive (e.g. #332)\n- some kind of comprehensive resource descriptor (e.g. bagit #828)\n- (partial) meta data summary in some kind of recognized format (e.g. ISATab for Scientific Data)\n\nAs any such use case could be arbitrarily complex and special, the solution could be a \"plugin\" interface, where more-or-less standalone scripts can be called trough a standard API.","files":null}]}